What upstream lacks (hermes-agent v0.22.5, apps/desktop/electron/main.ts):
renderer routing for a `hermes://session/<id>` deep link. main.ts already
finds a hermes:// token in the cold-start argv and in a second launch's
argv, parses it and queues it until the renderer is ready, but the
renderer's deep-link listener (use-desktop-integrations.ts,
lib/deeplink-routes.ts) handles mcp, blueprint, connections, plugin and
skill links, not `session`, so a `session` payload is dropped. This hunk sends a `session`
payload to 'hermes:focus-session' instead, the notification-click channel
the renderer answers by opening that chat.

A host launcher passes the URL as a positional
(packages/spaces-installer-session), the form upstream's own protocol
launch relies on. A switch such as `--session <id>` does not survive
Chromium's switches-first re-serialisation of a second launch's argv.

